# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# P6-4 (2026-09-29): do TAC DONGNG VAO cua bo tu dong vector hoa (P6).
#
# HAO HA: cap N VACH so sanh giua `k_p6_scalar.tkv` va `k_p6_vec.tkv` - hai
# file nay giong het nhau, cung du lieu, cung phep tinh, cung so lan lap.
# KHAC BIET DUY NHAT la dieu kien cua vong lap:
#
#   k_p6_vec.tkv     : `while i < nb`   -> `nb` la BIEN  -> P6 vector hoa
#   k_p6_scalar.tkv  : `while i < 262144` -> HANG SO     -> P6 TU CHOI
#
# Day khong phai so sanh cong khai giua hai thu bat ky: no so sanh CHINH
# compiler co bien dich vong lap nay hay khong, tren DUNG mot bien dich. Khong
# co y so nao khac chen gi vao giua - cung thuat toan, cung bo dem, cung du
# lieu, cung so vong lap. Chenh lech thoi gian do ra cong dung hieu qua cua P6.
#
# Dai do lon: N = 262144 = 2^18, chia het cho 4 nen khong con duoi scalar.
# R = 40 lan lap de thoi gian do duoc noi roi tren nhieu.
#
# `r` duoc tien vao bang -999.0 truoc moi lan lap: `Marshal.AllocHGlobal` tra ve
# vung nho CHUA khoi tao, nen neu vong lap bo sot phan tu, phan tu do giu gia
# tri cua lan truoc (cung la phep tinh dung) va checksum van khop - bien loi
# thanh khop. -999.0 khong the la ket qua dung cua phep cong nen lo ra ngay.
#
# Checksum lay mau MOT PHAN TU MOI 64 thay van tong ca N: tong day la vong lap
# SCALAR 262144 lan, se ngang nho voi phan tinh da duoc vector hoa va lam
# loe muc do. Dung sai o day la lo so (Sai so lam tron f32 don le), chu khong
# phai so sanh chinh xac tung phan tu - cai do Testkit da lo day kiem.

def main() -> "i32":
    n = 262144
    reps = 40
    a = f32buf(n)
    b = f32buf(n)
    r = f32buf(n)
    i = 0
    while i < n:
        a[i] = 1.5
        i = i + 1
    i = 0
    while i < n:
        b[i] = 2.25
        i = i + 1
    i = 0
    while i < n:
        r[i] = -999.0
        i = i + 1
    # `nb` la bien - DAY la thu tach vector hoa.
    nb = n
    rep = 0
    while rep < reps:
        i = 0
        while i < nb:
            r[i] = a[i] + b[i]
            i = i + 1
        rep = rep + 1
    cs = 0.0
    i = 0
    while i < n:
        cs = cs + r[i]
        i = i + 64
    print("sum=" + str(cs))
    return 0
